# The libraries module: a module of GCSL's standard library, compiled into
# every build and loaded by a run that imports it (`import libraries`). It
# says what a host pinned of the libraries a workspace imports; GCSL itself
# pins none.
#
# - `Pinned`: a library pinned: its import `path`, `github.com/gcslib/gcc`;
#   `git`, the URL of the git repository it comes from; `dir`, the
#   directory in the repository that holds it, empty for the root; and
#   `commit`, the whole name of the commit pinned.
# - `context pinned_libraries`: each library the workspace imports that its
#   host pinned, as pekit pins them in `pekit.lock`; none under plain GCSL.
#   A library that takes what one of these repositories gives another way,
#   a git crate say, can check that the two are the same commit.
type Pinned = {path: String, git: String, dir: String, commit: String}

context pinned_libraries: List<Pinned> = []
